{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1458443-aberrant-scale-and-range","id":1458443,"title":"[Aberrant] Scale and Range","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-02T20:15:37-07:00","id":1458443,"title":"[Aberrant] Scale and Range","content":"How do you interpret range bands with regards to Scale? For example, the Growth power and range of things they throw might be as simple as scaling up the default ranges comparable to the new size of the character. But what about other things, like if you wanted to Scale up the Area tag for instance if for some reason you had a character you wanted to be able to casually destroy larger areas like towns or even cities? Would you have it be purely narrative? A power stunt? <br /> <br /> Also, on the Moving and Maneuvering section in Core. It says that higher Scale (so Mega-Speed for example) can move up to two range bands relative to the lower Scale. So does that mean a Scale 1 can move Close Range and Scale 2 can move Medium Range, or is it the more reserved Scale 1 Close Range Scale 2 Short Range in a single turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T02:19:02-07:00","id":1458485,"title":"","content":"You can deal with it is 3 ways.<br /> <br /> The increased size will generate a lot of damage to everything, that you may use Collateral damage, and if it\u2019s their intention to destroy things doubles the dice they are adding to the pool and follow the rules for collateral damage. It would give a lot of interesting ideas to narrate around.<br /> <br /> Second option is to let them use power stunts and maxing out when they want to cause destruction, adding the area tag.<br /> <br /> The last, and for sure the easier way it to use narrative scale (also known as \u201cthe way it should be used\u201d) and let they narrate the chaos they are doing. If it\u2019s a NPC you can just do it for as long the characters don\u2019t interact with the NPC.<br /> <br /> Now on Speed Scale, the idea is kind of simple, the character can move their speed scale range bands as part of the action which no roll (except if there is a barrier or condition that says not) and can move 1 more range band if use an Athletics + physical attribute to do so, like sprinting for a short time or running while doing other actions. So scale 1 can move close or short, scale 2 can move short or medium, scale 3 can move medium or long, etc.<br /> <br /> I allow a higher scale to move longer distances when using dive for cover and roll away defensive stunts. So a Speed scale 4 can outrun a bullet by running to far to the bullet hit them (can run to long range while a pistol maximum range is medium), and a scale 2 can jump behind a car that is short range when diving for cover instead of just close range. This is not clear in the book, but I really think it\u2019s cool and follow the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-03-2021, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}